<title>JAPAN: Moody's keeps Sega's long-term debt rating at Baa2.</title>
<headline>Moody's keeps Sega's long-term debt rating at Baa2.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Thursday that it would keep Sega Enterprises Ltd's long-term debt rating at Baa2.  </p>
<p>Moody's action was based on the announcement earlier this week that the planned merger of Sega and Bandai Co Ltd was cancelled, the rating agency said.</p>
<p>Moody's had placed Sega's rating under review for a possible downgrade after the two companies' announcement in January that they would merge on October 1.</p>
<p>Moody's does not rate Bandai.</p>
</text>
